{"node":{"id":"HP:0025179","label":"Ground-glass opacification","ic":5.997,"definition":"On chest radiographs, ground-glass opacity appears as an area of hazy increased lung opacity, usually extensive, within which margins of pulmonary vessels may be indistinct. On CT scans, it appears as hazy increased opacity of lung, with preservation of bronchial and vascular margins. It is caused by partial filling of airspaces, interstitial thickening (due to fluid, cells, and/or fibrosis), partial collapse of alveoli, increased capillary blood volume, or a combination of these, the common factor being the partial displacement of air. Ground-glass opacity is less opaque than consolidation, in which bronchovascular margins are obscured."},"diseases":[{"id":"MONDO:0012650","label":"Cernunnos-XLF deficiency","in_core":false,"edge":{"id":"e_6487517cca64","source":"MONDO:0012650","target":"HP:0025179","type":"has_phenotype","evidence":[{"db":"HPO","origin":"OMIM","record":"OMIM:611291 · PMID:37703920","url":"https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/37703920/","level":"observed","date":"2025-12-22","confidence":1.0,"snippet":"Immunodeficiency 124, severe combined: Ground-glass opacification (frequency 1/1) [PCS]"}],"contradicting":[],"confidence":1.0,"independent_sources":["OMIM"],"level":"observed"},"confidence":1.0},{"id":"MONDO:0030692","label":"immunodeficiency 95","in_core":false,"edge":{"id":"e_0c956bb29289","source":"MONDO:0030692","target":"HP:0025179","type":"has_phenotype","evidence":[{"db":"HPO","origin":"OMIM","record":"OMIM:619773 · PMID:28606988","url":"https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/28606988/","level":"observed","date":"2022-05-29","confidence":1.0,"snippet":"Immunodeficiency 95: Ground-glass opacification (frequency 1/1) [PCS]"}],"contradicting":[],"confidence":1.0,"independent_sources":["OMIM"],"level":"observed"},"confidence":1.0},{"id":"MONDO:0800504","label":"idiopathic pulmonary fibrosis","in_core":false,"edge":{"id":"e_b7d65bc2f035","source":"MONDO:0800504","target":"H